UObjectToolTips.PythonScriptLibrary:AddAdditionalPath:
Add the given path to sys.path.
@note This API is designed to add paths outside of the standard UE paths (eg, a plugin that downloads Python scripts to a scratch location), and each path can only have a single owner.
      If the path being added already exists in sys.path then this function will return false, and the requested path is NOT tracked to your owner, and MAY be removed at any point in the future.

@param Path                          The path to add to sys.path; this must be an absolute path that exists on disk!
@param Owner                         An optional name to identify what owns this path (eg, the plugin or system name).
@param MountPointRoot        An optional and valid FPackageName root mount point (eg, "/MyPlugin/Python/AdditionalStuff") to allow types generated from this additional path to have stable names
                                                     (eg, "/MyPlugin/Python/AdditionalStuff/MyPythonClass_PY.MyPythonClass"), rather than unstable names (eg, "/Engine/PythonTypes.MyPythonClass_0x12345678")

@return True if the path was added, or false if it was invalid or already existed on sys.path.

