UObjectToolTips.PhysicsControlComponent:InvokeControlPro:
Looks up the profile which should exist in the registered control profile asset, and invokes it.

@param ProfileName The name of the control profile to apply
@param ControlSetMask The optional name of a control set to use as a mask, so only controls
       within that set will be modified. Standard control set names will include "All",
       "WorldSpace", "ParentSpace" and things like "WorldSpace_ArmLeft", depending on how
       controls have been created. If unset or invalid, no mask will be applied.
@param BodyModifierSetMask The optional name of a body modifier set to use as a mask, so only
       body modifiers within that set will be modified. Standard body modifier sets will
       include "All" and things like "ArmLeft", depending on how body modifiers have been
       created. If unset or invalid, no mask will be applied.
@param bApplyConstraintProfile If true, then the constraint profile named by ConstraintProfile
       is applied to the physics asset constraints of the affected bodies (when being used with
       a skeletal mesh). The constraints affected are those of the bodies selected by
       BodyModifierSetMask (an empty mask means all bodies). If false, no constraint profile
       is applied (and ConstraintProfile is ignored).
@param ConstraintProfile The name of the constraint profile (as defined in the physics asset)
       to apply when bApplyConstraintProfile is true. If the profile name is empty, invalid, or
       missing on a given constraint, that constraint is set to its default profile.
@return true if successful, and false if the profile cannot be found.

